@module level2data ; Level 2
@about The level's body: the header the game reads at $C4AE, the sprites, the object table, the metatiles, the map, the wave script, the enemy kinds and their movement scripts, the two mover tables and the movers.
$C4AE b L2Header ; The level header: restart point, checkpoints and the pointers the game reads
> Restart column $00, restart wave $0000; checkpoint columns $06, $2B, $FF with wave entries $E8B1, $EA55, $EE60; objects $D372, map $E762, kinds $F197, movers $F4BF and $F4D3.
$C4AF L2RestartWave ; the wave entry a life restarts at (the game keeps its live copy here)
$C4B1 L2Checks ; three checkpoint columns (CheckRestart)
$C4B4 L2WaveStarts ; the wave entries of the start and the checkpoints
$C4BA L2Pointers ; objects, map, kinds, movers 1, movers 2
$C4C4 b L2Spare ; zeros up to the sprites
$C4E0 b L2Sprites 9 ; The level's sprites: cells of 9 bytes (attribute, 8 pixel bytes) the object table points at
@res levels/level2/sprites.bin
$D372 b L2Objects 4 ; The level's object table: width, height, the cells' address (LevelObject)
@res levels/level2/objects.bin
$D442 b L2Metatiles 9 ; The metatiles, 144 bytes each (4 x 4 cells of 9 bytes), numbered down from the map: metatile n at $E762 - 144 x (n + 1) (MetatileAddress); 34 of them
@res levels/level2/metatiles.bin
$E762 b L2Map 5 ; The map: 5 bytes a block column (67 columns), each byte a metatile (bits 0-5) and its drawer (bits 6-7)
@res levels/level2/map.bin
$E8B1 b L2Waves ; The wave script: entries (scroll position, kind, script) RunWaves starts; then the enemies' movement scripts
@res levels/level2/waves.bin
